{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact head 72be89cca731241dbb36430fb5b99aa151fb942c, its one artifact `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md`, for request 66a5aa69 under implementation promise 2d860ac5 and my promise 60bc1375. The five rulings appear where they belong, and their text agrees with the rulings as filed. One sentence in section 17 contradicts the new status line.\n\nRequired change:\n\n- Section 17 ends with \"The note itself waits for review and for Hugh's ratification.\" (line 970). The new status line says that Hugh ratified the note and that it landed as main `270dc8c7`. Delete the sentence, or replace it with the fact. The change alters no decision of section 17.\n\nWhat I checked, item by item:\n\n1. The rulings, each in the section that it changes:\n   - `fa103f71`. Section 3 defines the version as the SHA-256 of the canonical bytes of `kind`, `on`, `fields` and `expected`, with each symbolic name as written, and says that the caller chooses the key. Section 5.3 adds `source` to the admitted `Exploration` and a paragraph that matches items 1, 2, 4 and 6: no authority, nothing retained, the version computed from the bound act, and `opens` and each symbolic name using the source. Section 8.1 says that `output(a)` names a source and leaves to E5 how a composition gives each step its key. Item 5 makes the key required and leaves `opens` without a value when no key is given. The note says that Explore takes a key and does not state either point. One sentence would cover it. I do not require it.\n   - `ef1fc932`. Section 5.4 names the three needs of the signed intent: the digest read by a guard or an effect, the cause of a creation send, and the whole signed input of a Native rule. It lists `create-room` of the Grow site as the one act of Grow, Lending and Counter that this rule makes `unavailable`. That matches the builder's audit a11ef5df, which finds the other `unavailable` acts in `examples/repo-in-ai` and none in Lending or Counter.\n   - `04218678`. Section 5.4 gives a `device-command` record the name `{ entry: Source }` and says that `set-fan`, `set-heater`, `set-vent` and `authorize` are judged, with the exact count of records and the exact reservations in the hypothetical view.\n   - `18a41f8f`. Section 5.4 adds a fourth `unavailable` case for a hold workspace that would write a derived record or an operation. The ruling's list of affected acts belongs to the E1 implementation note, not this note.\n   - `99506fe3`. Section 5.1 states that the contract covers the judge's answer and not the scope's capacity, that the scope can refuse an admitted act with `scope-full`, and that a page reads room from Observe (section 5.5).\n   - Section 18 lists the five rulings with the sections that they change, and the request IDs of E1 to E6, R, A and the review after E3.\n2. The status line is true. Main `270dc8c7` holds the note at f760e371, the head that I approved in 813ce2a5, and Hugh's ratification 9eec86a8 precedes it. Line 970 is the one sentence that contradicts it.\n3. The diff touches no line of section 13 or of the decisions in section 17.\n\nScope. The head's one parent is main `0166423a`, and it changes one path. `git ls-remote origin` shows no branch `planner/act-environment-amend-20261114`, so I read the head from the shared object store. Push the corrected head before the landing. Under the notes-only rule of `docs/testing.md` the head runs no test, and I ran none.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The key belongs to the caller and the version to Explore, so a caller cannot name a version that Explore did not compute. The capacity boundary keeps Explore to the judge's answer and adds no second copy of the turn's admission.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The key carries no authority. Each new `unavailable` case refuses instead of inventing an intent, a cause or an identifier.\n\nSimplification: no required change beyond the one sentence.\n\nThe planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca9